title: 'First M1.0 probe results on macOS: sandbox argv leak via sysmond, escapes found, Noise passes'
summary: |-
  First real probe results on macOS 15.7.3 arm64, Node 26.

  p10m-sbx-deny-mac FAIL:
  - The endpoint-port deny holds (curl, net, WS, ::1).
  - The specified process-info deny does NOT hide other processes' argv: pgrep reads it via the root sysmond daemon over XPC. Fix: deny mach-lookup com.apple.sysmond.
  - Same-user signals to the kernel are not covered by any rule.
  - /bin/ps cannot run under any sandbox-exec profile (setuid).
  - tmux and screen escapes reach the denied port; unix-socket denies close them.
  - The LaunchServices `open` escape reaches the denied port, and no SBPL fix was found, so it is a residual.

  p11-ws-framing PARTIAL: framing passes (9 API + 27 raw cases), throughput ~620-730 MB/s, but peak RSS is 200-248 MB against a 60 MB bar while phys_footprint is 39.8 MB. The criterion must name its metric.

  p-noise-vectors PASS: 5 published cacophony/snow vectors (IK, XX, XXpsk3) over node:crypto only.

  p01-claude-cli PARTIAL: claude 2.1.302 has all 12 flags; --setting-sources lists only user/project/local (no managed); live checks remain manual.

  Spec corrections are owed for §11.2 2b(b), §15.1 row 19, §15.5, §16, G-SBX-08, §A.2, the P11 metric and the §3.3 managed layer. The founder's Mac ran throwaway .app registrations and a hidden Calculator launch once (cleaned up).
symbols_touched:
  - '#gnomon-probes'
  - '#paradigm-harness'
learnings:
  - 'On macOS, process-info sandbox denies don''t hide the process table: entitled tools (pgrep) fetch it from the root sysmond daemon over XPC, so the mach-lookup for com.apple.sysmond must be denied too.'
  - ps/getrusage RSS overstates Node memory on macOS (it keeps freed pages); use phys_footprint for memory budgets.
verification:
  status: partial
  details:
    pass:
      - p-noise-vectors
    partial:
      - p11-ws-framing
      - p01-claude-cli
    fail:
      - p10m-sbx-deny-mac
